00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:58.620
In 1929, the Dow fell 89% over three years after margin-fueled speculation collapsed, with recovery taking until 1954.

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:10.820
Black Monday in 1987 saw a 22.6% single-day drop triggered by program trading and portfolio insurance, yet the index regained its level within two years.

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:23.360
The .com bust erased 78% from the NASDAQ between 2000 and 2002 after speculative valuations detached from earnings, with full recovery stretching seven years.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:34.660
The 2008 crisis produced a 57% S&amp;P 500 decline amid housing leverage and bank failures, requiring four years to return to prior highs.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:45.340
COVID's 34% plunge in March 2020 lasted only 23 trading days before new highs, aided by instant fiscal and monetary support.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:53.460
What most retail investors miss is that every crash featured a preceding period of compressed volatility and rising leverage.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:59.760
The professionals always check margin debt levels and VIX term structure before sizing new positions.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:05.520
The biggest mistake with crash preparation is assuming the next event will match the last one.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:13.780
Instead, always maintain a written reentry plan tied to fixed percentage drawdown thresholds, rather than trying to time the bottom.

